1274
00:54:12.630 --> 00:54:14.630
I never tore off that first page.

1275
00:54:14.630 --> 00:54:15.770
And I still have it.

1276
00:54:15.870 --> 00:54:17.610
And the whole notepad is unused.

1277
00:54:17.950 --> 00:54:22.570
And that first page just has all of Sprinkles, like medicines and how to care for her.

1278
00:54:23.770 --> 00:54:25.170
Oh, my gosh.

1279
00:54:25.450 --> 00:54:25.990
Oh, look.

1280
00:54:26.070 --> 00:54:26.350
Oh, wait.

1281
00:54:26.430 --> 00:54:27.350
Oh, I took a picture of it.

1282
00:54:27.430 --> 00:54:27.970
Do you want to see?

1283
00:54:28.570 --> 00:54:28.970
Yeah.

1284
00:54:29.450 --> 00:54:29.890
Okay, here.

1285
00:54:30.150 --> 00:54:31.010
That is amazing.

1286
00:54:31.030 --> 00:54:32.190
But that's not your handwriting.

1287
00:54:32.370 --> 00:54:33.050
No, no, no.

1288
00:54:33.050 --> 00:54:33.990
It's not my handwriting.

1289
00:54:34.190 --> 00:54:36.070
Someone in the props department wrote that out.

1290
00:54:36.590 --> 00:54:36.990
Wow.

1291
00:54:37.650 --> 00:54:39.130
We have to post that on the pod.

1292
00:54:39.310 --> 00:54:40.290
We'll post it on the pod.

1293
00:54:40.470 --> 00:54:40.610
Okay.

1294
00:54:41.010 --> 00:54:42.630
Sprinkles medication going on the pod.

1295
00:54:45.330 --> 00:54:50.190
Well, we got a fan question from Tracy Prescott, who said this.

1296
00:54:50.470 --> 00:54:53.730
I am a cat-focused veterinarian in Atlanta.

1297
00:54:54.070 --> 00:55:00.790
And I was wondering if an actual doctor of veterinary medicine was consulted about Sprinkles medical needs

1298
00:55:00.790 --> 00:55:05.870
because Angela's list of medications and treatments she gave to Dwight were very realistic.

1299
00:55:05.870 --> 00:55:07.950
Oh, that's fantastic.

1300
00:55:08.950 --> 00:55:14.190
Well, Greg told me that he had the writer's assistants, Nate Fetterman and Jonathan Hughes,

1301
00:55:14.510 --> 00:55:17.170
do research into the accurate cat medicines.

1302
00:55:17.270 --> 00:55:21.690
And that is why that list of medicines is so realistic.

1303
00:55:21.950 --> 00:55:23.710
Well, good job, writer's assistants.

1304
00:55:24.250 --> 00:55:25.230
That's right.

1305
00:55:25.230 --> 00:55:36.130
Well, listen, before we go on, maybe we should take a break because coming up, Michael is going to try to, I don't know, right this wrong.

1306
00:55:36.510 --> 00:55:37.650
He's going to try.

1307
00:55:37.650 --> 00:55:39.170
It's not going to go well.

1308
00:55:39.610 --> 00:55:40.830
It never does.

1309
00:55:41.070 --> 00:55:41.270
No.

1310
00:55:41.850 --> 00:55:42.510
All right.

1311
00:55:42.510 --> 00:55:43.230
We'll be back.

1312
00:55:43.450 --> 00:55:52.200
All right.

1313
00:55:52.200 --> 00:55:53.200
We are back.

1314
00:55:53.340 --> 00:56:01.780
And Angela, Michael has gone into the break room in an attempt to rally everyone to plant a tree in honor of Meredith.

1315
00:56:02.440 --> 00:56:04.680
But do you know what I titled this scene?

1316
00:56:04.820 --> 00:56:08.120
You are always titling scenes and I have titled a scene.

1317
00:56:09.640 --> 00:56:11.280
John eats popcorn.

1318
00:56:11.840 --> 00:56:13.060
Oh, my gosh.

1319
00:56:13.860 --> 00:56:18.120
Did you notice he is eating popcorn through this whole scene?

1320
00:56:18.280 --> 00:56:20.840
Not carrots, not baby carrots, but popcorn.

1321
00:56:20.980 --> 00:56:26.660
And the way he's eating it, it's so, it's so delicate.

1322
00:56:27.360 --> 00:56:29.840
Was he trying not to crunch too loudly?

1323
00:56:30.240 --> 00:56:37.200
I think he was trying not to be a problem for sound, but he was clearly hungry because he eats it through the whole scene.

1324
00:56:37.460 --> 00:56:38.240
Oh, my God.

1325
00:56:38.240 --> 00:56:42.240
Was this the year we got that little popcorn maker by Kraft Services?

1326
00:56:43.400 --> 00:56:44.560
It must have been.

1327
00:56:44.780 --> 00:56:47.520
This must have been the first week with the popcorn maker.

1328
00:56:47.520 --> 00:56:52.460
We went a little crazy for popcorn, and then the sound department, I think, said, okay, guys.

1329
00:56:53.040 --> 00:56:54.520
I remember it went away.

1330
00:56:54.740 --> 00:56:54.880
Yeah.

1331
00:56:55.100 --> 00:56:56.800
But we were excited about it.

1332
00:56:57.000 --> 00:57:04.640
Well, he's eating popcorn in this whole scene, and it's also in this scene that Pam explains to Michael, you know, we're just going to go visit Meredith.

1333
00:57:04.640 --> 00:57:07.380
We're going to go in shifts so we don't overwhelm her.

1334
00:57:07.380 --> 00:57:10.560
But Michael is like, no, we're all going together.

1335
00:57:10.560 --> 00:57:12.440
At the same time, I'll drive.

1336
00:57:12.740 --> 00:57:16.240
So Jim and Pam are like, well, we can each take people in our separate cars.

1337
00:57:16.380 --> 00:57:18.140
And Oscar's like, separate cars?

1338
00:57:18.320 --> 00:57:21.360
And Kevin's like, I don't believe it.

1339
00:57:21.680 --> 00:57:22.300
I know.

1340
00:57:22.600 --> 00:57:28.020
Well, then Michael has a talking head, and he says, you know, I have flaws, you know, so sue me.

1341
00:57:28.080 --> 00:57:29.380
And he's like, no, no, no, don't sue me.

1342
00:57:29.680 --> 00:57:36.960
But Jenna, there was an alt to this talking head, and it's in the deleted scenes, and it made me laugh so hard.

1343
00:57:36.960 --> 00:57:40.640
And it's also in the bloopers, and Steve couldn't get through it.

1344
00:57:40.720 --> 00:57:41.400
He kept laughing.

1345
00:57:42.080 --> 00:57:42.980
What is it?

1346
00:57:43.020 --> 00:57:43.400
Okay.

1347
00:57:43.800 --> 00:57:45.180
This is it.

1348
00:57:45.260 --> 00:57:45.960
There's one take.

1349
00:57:46.140 --> 00:57:48.460
Clearly, he got through it because it's in the deleted scenes.

1350
00:57:48.940 --> 00:57:51.800
He says, I am not a bad guy.

1351
00:57:52.240 --> 00:57:55.480
I am a good guy who runs over women with his car.

1352
00:57:56.600 --> 00:57:59.620
Why am I having such a hard time getting my message across?

1353
00:58:00.680 --> 00:58:01.800
Oh, my gosh.

1354
00:58:01.820 --> 00:58:02.620
That is funny.

1355
00:58:03.140 --> 00:58:05.840
And the way Steve does it is so good.

1356
00:58:05.840 --> 00:58:06.940
That's good.

1357
00:58:07.180 --> 00:58:08.240
I have to go watch that.

1358
00:58:08.280 --> 00:58:08.980
Yeah, you have to.

1359
00:58:09.500 --> 00:58:15.880
Well, we don't find out exactly how they get there, but the entire gang does arrive at the hospital.

1360
00:58:16.140 --> 00:58:18.660
Michael has a whole bunch of balloons.

1361
00:58:18.740 --> 00:58:20.700
And the entire gang minus Dwight.

1362
00:58:21.700 --> 00:58:25.680
That's right, because Dwight has gone to take care of Sprinkles.

1363
00:58:27.020 --> 00:58:36.900
Everyone gathers around Meredith's bed, and we talked about this scene with Kate, about how Steve improvised crawling on top of her in that one moment.

1364
00:58:36.900 --> 00:58:38.940
He's, like, trying to give her a hug.

1365
00:58:39.240 --> 00:58:40.420
It's pretty amazing.

1366
00:58:40.740 --> 00:58:41.200
It's pretty great.

1367
00:58:41.200 --> 00:58:50.800
There is a deleted scene from this moment where Creed, as they're exiting, just grabs all her meds out of the little plastic cups they're sitting on her tray.

1368
00:58:51.180 --> 00:58:51.640
Oh.

1369
00:58:51.800 --> 00:58:53.740
And Creed just pockets all her meds.

1370
00:58:54.940 --> 00:58:56.100
Of course he does.

1371
00:58:56.860 --> 00:59:02.940
Well, I had a favorite moment from this scene, and I wanted to ask you about it because I think maybe you improvised it.

1372
00:59:02.940 --> 00:59:14.960
When Michael is trying to get Meredith to forgive him, he says that she should think about the Bible because it says that forgiveness is next to godliness.

1373
00:59:15.740 --> 00:59:18.120
And you mutter, that's cleanliness.

1374
00:59:18.940 --> 00:59:20.080
I did improvise that.

1375
00:59:21.820 --> 00:59:28.340
Oh, I also wanted to mention in this scene the nurse, who is an improv person from IO.

1376
00:59:28.340 --> 00:59:30.160
Her name is Sylvia McClure.

1377
00:59:31.060 --> 00:59:34.320
Well, I looked at her IMDb, and I found this very interesting.

1378
00:59:34.940 --> 00:59:45.320
In addition to playing a nurse on The Office, she has also played a doctor on Young and the Restless, Dexter and Intelligence, a nurse in Night of the Dead,

1379
00:59:45.440 --> 00:59:47.560
and a receptionist nurse on The Unit.

1380
00:59:48.760 --> 00:59:52.040
So she's played a lot of nurses and doctors.

1381
00:59:52.200 --> 00:59:54.760
And incidentally, she's also twice been cast as a nun.

1382
00:59:55.540 --> 00:59:57.180
That is very interesting.

1383
00:59:57.180 --> 01:00:00.740
Like, sort of a, it's like a weird typecasting.

1384
01:00:01.460 --> 01:00:03.020
Yeah, exactly.

1385
01:00:03.020 --> 01:00:08.260
Well, I used to get a lot of auditions for school teachers and nurses.

1386
01:00:08.600 --> 01:00:10.600
Have you ever played a nurse or doctor?

1387
01:00:11.220 --> 01:00:12.480
Yes, actually.

1388
01:00:12.620 --> 01:00:17.840
I played a pediatric nurse in this movie called The Promotion.

1389
01:00:17.840 --> 01:00:30.580
I played a doctor on an episode of Monk, and I played a sexy nurse briefly in one of our Halloween episodes of The Office.

1390
01:00:31.740 --> 01:00:35.700
What were you most often typecast as for auditions?

1391
01:00:36.440 --> 01:00:37.940
Before The Office?

1392
01:00:38.160 --> 01:00:39.660
Before The Office.

1393
01:00:40.020 --> 01:00:40.760
Quirky.

1394
01:00:41.020 --> 01:00:41.820
Quirky gal.

1395
01:00:42.060 --> 01:00:42.720
What's up?

1396
01:00:42.780 --> 01:00:44.440
My quirky, quirky fun neighbor.

1397
01:00:44.540 --> 01:00:45.260
Quirky neighbor.

1398
01:00:45.740 --> 01:00:46.440
Yeah.

1399
01:00:48.360 --> 01:00:55.260
Yeah, I was, I got a lot of just the school teachers, waitresses, and nurses.

1400
01:00:56.300 --> 01:01:03.180
Well, I will tell you, we talked about how hard we laughed in this scene, but 11 minutes, 22 seconds is when you can see us breaking.

1401
01:01:03.520 --> 01:01:07.620
If you're looking for it, that's when Michael crawls on top of Meredith.

1402
01:01:08.240 --> 01:01:17.400
Well, now we can go back to The Office, and we are going to find Dwight telling Angela some bad news.

1403
01:01:17.400 --> 01:01:19.000
And she's anxious to see him.

1404
01:01:19.160 --> 01:01:20.640
She wants to know how it went.

1405
01:01:20.780 --> 01:01:21.700
You can just tell.

1406
01:01:22.120 --> 01:01:23.640
And then he's like, hey, monkey.

1407
01:01:23.820 --> 01:01:24.820
And she's like, any problems?

1408
01:01:25.220 --> 01:01:27.800
Well, you left the TV on, and your cat is dead.

1409
01:01:28.380 --> 01:01:30.740
And my character's like, what?

1410
01:01:31.120 --> 01:01:34.020
And he's like, Sparkles, the white one, is dead.

1411
01:01:34.380 --> 01:01:35.880
Yeah, he gets the name wrong.

1412
01:01:36.080 --> 01:01:36.740
It's bad.

1413
01:01:36.800 --> 01:01:37.560
It is bad.

1414
01:01:37.800 --> 01:01:39.300
This will not end well.

1415
01:01:40.040 --> 01:01:46.260
Angela, you get so very immediately emotional, and not in a funny way.

1416
01:01:46.440 --> 01:01:52.500
Like, this is one of the ways that our show allowed characters to be real people.

1417
01:01:53.000 --> 01:01:59.680
Because Angela, the character, really loved her cat, and she is heartbroken.

1418
01:02:00.040 --> 01:02:03.360
And you see that real pain here from your character.

1419
01:02:03.540 --> 01:02:05.680
How did you gear up for this scene?

1420
01:02:06.020 --> 01:02:09.200
Well, Greg told me, he said, you know, Angela Martin.

1421
01:02:09.300 --> 01:02:12.480
Hearing this news will be devastated.

1422
01:02:13.420 --> 01:02:20.600
And I need you to play out the beats of hearing news that kind of destroys you in the moment.

1423
01:02:20.780 --> 01:02:25.540
You know, and I feel like we've all had moments in our lives where we've gotten that phone call

1424
01:02:25.540 --> 01:02:27.780
with some bad news, you know, unfortunately.

1425
01:02:28.240 --> 01:02:36.060
And I just sort of thought about a few of those moments where, you know, at first, you're just

1426
01:02:36.060 --> 01:02:39.680
in total shock where you're not really sure what you heard.

1427
01:02:40.400 --> 01:02:40.940
Yeah.

1428
01:02:40.940 --> 01:02:44.660
And then it's like someone slaps you in the face with the information.

1429
01:02:45.920 --> 01:02:49.260
And then you're trying to make sense of it, but you can't make sense of it.

1430
01:02:49.840 --> 01:02:51.120
It's the unthinkable.

1431
01:02:51.260 --> 01:02:52.680
And it doesn't make sense.

1432
01:02:53.000 --> 01:02:54.980
And your body is doing all of that.

1433
01:02:55.140 --> 01:02:56.100
You're in shock.

1434
01:02:56.300 --> 01:02:57.040
You're sad.

1435
01:02:57.540 --> 01:03:01.440
Your body, your mind is trying to make it right, but you can't make it right.

1436
01:03:01.460 --> 01:03:02.700
You can't figure it out.

1437
01:03:02.700 --> 01:03:04.340
You don't understand why it happened.

1438
01:03:04.800 --> 01:03:08.300
And I was just trying to process through all of that.

1439
01:03:08.720 --> 01:03:11.640
And yeah, that's what I did.

1440
01:03:11.860 --> 01:03:13.980
Did you have to do a lot of takes of that scene?

1441
01:03:13.980 --> 01:03:14.620
Do you remember?

1442
01:03:14.940 --> 01:03:15.860
No, I didn't.

1443
01:03:15.940 --> 01:03:17.200
I was thankful for that.

1444
01:03:17.520 --> 01:03:20.360
In the next scene, your character is still crying.

1445
01:03:20.540 --> 01:03:22.460
She's standing at reception with Pam.

1446
01:03:22.460 --> 01:03:26.740
And you look like you've been crying for a long time.

1447
01:03:27.200 --> 01:03:32.460
What did you do to get there, to start the scene in a place like that?

1448
01:03:32.460 --> 01:03:33.700
You know, I'm chatty.

1449
01:03:33.820 --> 01:03:40.060
So my instinct would be, I'm standing by reception with you, would be to be hanging out, you know, being part of the bullpen.

1450
01:03:40.280 --> 01:03:47.040
So one of the things I did was I went around the corner by the elevators by myself in between takes, and I did not hang out.

1451
01:03:47.260 --> 01:03:50.300
And I just tried to stay in sort of that sad space.

1452
01:03:51.980 --> 01:03:59.480
And also, the makeup department, they wanted my eyes to really look like I had bawled my eyes out.

1453
01:03:59.660 --> 01:04:00.540
And they did.

1454
01:04:00.540 --> 01:04:03.960
So I had to get myself back in that emotional place and get sad again.

1455
01:04:04.540 --> 01:04:16.200
And also, the makeup department, Kenneth Paul, who did my makeup, did like this type of eyeliner that really made the inside, it was like in the inside of your eye, reddish pink.

1456
01:04:16.200 --> 01:04:21.080
So my eyes, my eyes looked the part, and then emotionally, I got there.

1457
01:04:22.080 --> 01:04:25.620
Your eyes looked like you had three margaritas yesterday.

1458
01:04:27.020 --> 01:04:28.220
That's what you look like.

1459
01:04:28.260 --> 01:04:31.740
Maybe that's what I, that should have been my prep instead of eyeliner and sad thoughts.

1460
01:04:31.740 --> 01:04:40.600
But no, what happened was Laverne just showed Kenneth Paul a picture of me from the previous day and was like, make her look like that.

1461
01:04:41.040 --> 01:04:50.080
No, but in all seriousness, Angela, when I was watching these series of scenes where your character is really, really devastated over the death of Sprinkles,

1462
01:04:50.080 --> 01:04:57.960
I was just so beyond impressed with your performance and your range and your believability.

1463
01:04:58.400 --> 01:05:02.020
It was just, this is just great, great work.

1464
01:05:02.380 --> 01:05:03.120
Aw, thanks.

1465
01:05:03.420 --> 01:05:04.620
I appreciate that.

1466
01:05:04.840 --> 01:05:07.920
I really appreciated Greg writing the storyline for me.

1467
01:05:07.920 --> 01:05:17.080
And I got to do all these things, you know, and, and, you know, his take as a director was always to try to keep it as honest as possible.

1468
01:05:17.920 --> 01:05:18.440
Yeah.

1469
01:05:19.440 --> 01:05:26.860
Well, there's another really great moment in the scene, and we actually had a fan write in.

1470
01:05:27.120 --> 01:05:34.120
Katie Harwick said, I think we need to give a shout out to Michael when Angela's cat dies.

1471
01:05:34.120 --> 01:05:39.040
Not only did he know her name, but he was overcome with grief.

1472
01:05:39.340 --> 01:05:44.100
He cares so much for his employees, and it was just such a sweet moment to me.

1473
01:05:44.420 --> 01:05:53.960
But I do have to ask, do you think he was truly sad, or did he just see this as a distraction from hitting Meredith that everyone could talk about instead?

1474
01:05:54.520 --> 01:05:58.780
I personally think he was very distraught about Sprinkles.

1475
01:05:58.780 --> 01:06:00.140
Well, I agree.

1476
01:06:00.440 --> 01:06:06.340
This happens at 12 minutes, 41 seconds, and it is one of my favorite endearing moments of Michael.

1477
01:06:06.480 --> 01:06:10.500
Now, maybe because it's personal for me, because, you know, I played Angela Martin.

1478
01:06:10.620 --> 01:06:12.100
I knew how much she loved her cats.

1479
01:06:12.460 --> 01:06:18.660
But Michael, it's like that moment when the trick-or-treaters come to his house, and you see his joy.

1480
01:06:18.920 --> 01:06:22.660
It's like that moment when he shows up to Pam's art show.

1481
01:06:23.300 --> 01:06:23.640
Yeah.

1482
01:06:23.640 --> 01:06:27.240
Michael really saw these people as his family.

1483
01:06:27.500 --> 01:06:30.180
So Michael knew Angela's love of Sprinkles.

1484
01:06:30.300 --> 01:06:31.240
Of course he did.

1485
01:06:31.700 --> 01:06:32.260
Yeah.

1486
01:06:32.260 --> 01:06:35.020
And he was gutted to hear that Sprinkles died.

1487
01:06:35.200 --> 01:06:41.440
The way he puts his hand up to his face, and he kind of collapses into the wall, and he's like, oh, shoot.

1488
01:06:41.840 --> 01:06:43.480
I'm sorry, Angela.

1489
01:06:43.860 --> 01:06:46.340
I mean, could it get any worse?

1490
01:06:47.020 --> 01:06:48.520
He's feeling all of that.

1491
01:06:48.520 --> 01:06:49.980
He really feels bad.

1492
01:06:54.280 --> 01:06:56.980
And then he makes a big speech and calls her Prinkles.

1493
01:06:57.300 --> 01:06:57.960
So, you know.

1494
01:06:58.080 --> 01:06:58.500
He does.

1495
01:06:59.200 --> 01:07:00.040
That's right.

1496
01:07:00.320 --> 01:07:04.460
He says, so many bad things have happened today.

1497
01:07:04.860 --> 01:07:10.720
The computer crashes from porn, merit of this accident, and now Prinkles.

1498
01:07:11.020 --> 01:07:11.760
We're cursed.

1499
01:07:12.040 --> 01:07:13.620
This seals the deal.

1500
01:07:14.000 --> 01:07:15.800
To him, that's it.

1501
01:07:15.900 --> 01:07:20.040
The office is cursed, and now he's got to figure out how to break this curse.

1502
01:07:20.040 --> 01:07:24.840
Yes, but he does say, I'm not superstitious, but I am a little stitious.

1503
01:07:25.880 --> 01:07:28.260
It's like he thinks they're two separate words.

1504
01:07:28.540 --> 01:07:34.340
Well, we had a fan question about that line from Jessica Williard and Lauren Corwin.

1505
01:07:34.860 --> 01:07:38.160
They said, that line makes me laugh every time.

1506
01:07:39.060 --> 01:07:40.660
Who wrote this joke?

1507
01:07:40.880 --> 01:07:42.060
I was curious, too.

1508
01:07:42.200 --> 01:07:42.980
Did you find out?

1509
01:07:43.340 --> 01:07:44.080
I did.

1510
01:07:44.340 --> 01:07:45.740
It was Gene Stepnitsky.

1511
01:07:46.000 --> 01:07:47.400
Gene, hilarious.

1512
01:07:48.060 --> 01:07:52.540
Yeah, I asked Greg, and he said, I'm pretty sure it was Gene or Lee.

1513
01:07:52.760 --> 01:07:54.240
I reached out to those guys.

1514
01:07:54.460 --> 01:07:56.560
Gene said, yes, it was me.

1515
01:07:56.780 --> 01:07:57.460
He remembers.

1516
01:07:57.760 --> 01:08:03.140
They were in a group, and this talking head leads to a commercial break.

1517
01:08:03.340 --> 01:08:04.780
And they needed a button.

1518
01:08:05.080 --> 01:08:10.260
They needed a little button at the end of this talking head so that they could go to commercial.

1519
01:08:10.560 --> 01:08:15.180
And he said they were just trying to come up with something, and all of a sudden he said,

1520
01:08:15.180 --> 01:08:16.820
he shouted out, I've got it.

1521
01:08:17.020 --> 01:08:20.220
This might be stupid, but how about this?

1522
01:08:20.620 --> 01:08:24.180
And he pitched that line, and it is so genius.

1523
01:08:24.400 --> 01:08:28.080
It is such a good line, and I hear that line quoted all the time.

1524
01:08:28.200 --> 01:08:30.140
It is a Michael Scott classic line.

1525
01:08:30.600 --> 01:08:31.300
It is.

1526
01:08:31.400 --> 01:08:31.960
It's true.

1527
01:08:32.720 --> 01:08:39.120
Well, speaking of classic Michael Scott, we're now going to move into one of Michael's conference room meetings.

1528
01:08:39.120 --> 01:08:41.860
This is an epic conference room meeting.

1529
01:08:42.040 --> 01:08:44.460
We were in this conference room all freaking day.

1530
01:08:44.900 --> 01:08:46.220
We got loopy.

1531
01:08:46.380 --> 01:08:47.200
We got punchy.

1532
01:08:47.320 --> 01:08:49.660
I'm going to tell you where we flat out lost it.

1533
01:08:50.120 --> 01:08:51.220
It's so good.

1534
01:08:51.500 --> 01:08:51.800
Yeah.

1535
01:08:51.960 --> 01:08:59.140
I also remember that they very specifically did not seat Jim and Pam next to one another.

1536
01:08:59.300 --> 01:09:05.580
This was part of Jim and Pam's supposed way of deflecting that we're dating.

1537
01:09:06.300 --> 01:09:06.840
Yeah.

1538
01:09:06.840 --> 01:09:11.540
And I remember that you have to just be sad and kind of cry through this scene,

1539
01:09:11.540 --> 01:09:16.960
and that I didn't want to chat you up too much because I knew you had to stay in that space.

1540
01:09:17.160 --> 01:09:18.020
And I did.

1541
01:09:18.160 --> 01:09:18.760
I did.

1542
01:09:19.240 --> 01:09:23.860
I really stayed sad until the end when Steve made me break into laughter.

1543
01:09:24.120 --> 01:09:26.620
So Michael in this scene is questioning his employees.

1544
01:09:26.720 --> 01:09:30.380
He feels like someone must have done something to get this curse, right?

1545
01:09:30.560 --> 01:09:34.060
Like, have they violated an ancient Indian burial ground?

1546
01:09:34.060 --> 01:09:38.960
And then, you know, he wants to know what everyone's religious beliefs are.

1547
01:09:39.160 --> 01:09:42.500
Which Toby says, Michael, we can't, you can't do that.

1548
01:09:42.660 --> 01:09:43.680
You can't discuss that.

1549
01:09:43.940 --> 01:09:47.120
Michael calls Toby Satan repeatedly in this scene.

1550
01:09:47.820 --> 01:09:50.220
One, because he won a week of free pizza.

1551
01:09:50.220 --> 01:09:51.760
So he's like, I don't think there's a curse.

1552
01:09:51.760 --> 01:09:53.260
And Michael's like, okay, Satan.

1553
01:09:53.720 --> 01:09:55.400
So he goes around the room.

1554
01:09:55.620 --> 01:09:57.860
Pam and Daryl are both Presbyterians.

1555
01:09:58.100 --> 01:09:58.780
They high five.

1556
01:09:59.540 --> 01:10:04.020
Phyllis has this great line where she says, I'm a Lutheran and Bob is a Unitarian.

1557
01:10:04.320 --> 01:10:05.560
Keeps things spicy.

1558
01:10:06.660 --> 01:10:07.080
Mm-hmm.

1559
01:10:07.680 --> 01:10:11.260
Creed said he's been a follower in a cult and a leader in a cult.

1560
01:10:11.460 --> 01:10:13.980
The followers have more fun, but the leaders make more money.

1561
01:10:13.980 --> 01:10:19.620
But Michael has decided, he thinks, maybe we should do an animal sacrifice.

1562
01:10:19.900 --> 01:10:20.340
Yes.

1563
01:10:20.460 --> 01:10:20.680
You know?

1564
01:10:20.800 --> 01:10:21.740
That's going to do it.

1565
01:10:21.780 --> 01:10:22.440
Maybe that would help.

1566
01:10:22.600 --> 01:10:22.820
Yeah.

1567
01:10:22.940 --> 01:10:23.200
Mm-hmm.

1568
01:10:23.480 --> 01:10:29.040
And then he starts naming animals, but they don't exiSt.

1569
01:10:29.420 --> 01:10:30.600
I wrote them down.

1570
01:10:30.600 --> 01:10:59.600
He suggests that we sacrifice an animal that has the body of a walrus and the head of a sea lion or the body of an egret with the head of a meerkat or maybe one that has the head of a monkey with the antlers of a reindeer and the body of a porcupine.

1571
01:10:59.600 --> 01:11:04.780
Okay, Jenna, when Steve started this runner, they just let him go.

1572
01:11:05.000 --> 01:11:05.900
Do you remember this?

1573
01:11:06.100 --> 01:11:06.300
Yes.

1574
01:11:06.360 --> 01:11:10.180
He just started improvising different animal combinations.

1575
01:11:10.580 --> 01:11:13.580
We didn't know what was going to come out of the guy's mouth.

1576
01:11:13.600 --> 01:11:18.140
We all started dropping like flies, cracking up.

1577
01:11:18.260 --> 01:11:21.600
And the other thing is, he would say it with such seriousness.

1578
01:11:22.080 --> 01:11:27.240
And this was the comedy killer, the long pauses.

1579
01:11:27.240 --> 01:11:33.160
He takes such a long pause before he says, body of a porcupine?

1580
01:11:33.660 --> 01:11:34.260
Yes.

1581
01:11:34.480 --> 01:11:35.320
We were on the floor.

1582
01:11:35.540 --> 01:11:36.900
We were on the floor.

1583
01:11:37.080 --> 01:11:42.700
I am not in any background shots while he's doing these animal combinations because I couldn't keep it together.

1584
01:11:43.260 --> 01:11:48.960
And at 18 minutes, 11 seconds, you can see Craig Robinson covering his face.

1585
01:11:49.260 --> 01:11:50.380
I saw it.

1586
01:11:50.680 --> 01:11:51.940
I remember that.

1587
01:11:52.540 --> 01:11:54.560
We were losing it.

1588
01:11:55.240 --> 01:11:57.880
It was so funny.

1589
01:11:58.120 --> 01:12:00.660
And they let him go for a long time.

1590
01:12:01.180 --> 01:12:03.440
I mean, you are not seeing all of it.

1591
01:12:03.560 --> 01:12:05.320
He went for so long.

1592
01:12:05.500 --> 01:12:11.120
And I remember we were cracking up and we were just like, as a group, we were like, no, get it together.

1593
01:12:11.300 --> 01:12:12.140
These are too good.

1594
01:12:12.240 --> 01:12:13.160
We can't ruin these.

1595
01:12:13.160 --> 01:12:19.160
Well, while all this is happening at the office, Dwight has gone to visit Meredith.

1596
01:12:19.760 --> 01:12:31.560
And he has this talking head where he's saying, as he's sitting next to her, that sometimes the best thing to do is to put an animal out of its misery.

1597
01:12:31.920 --> 01:12:32.780
He's a farmer.

1598
01:12:33.040 --> 01:12:33.400
Yeah.

1599
01:12:33.780 --> 01:12:38.760
You could power a small fan for two days with the amount of electricity Meredith is hooked up to.

1600
01:12:39.520 --> 01:12:53.760
I have to say, please, if you go back to rewatch this episode, during this speech by Dwight, next to Meredith's bedside, please look at the woman in the bed on the other side.

1601
01:12:54.640 --> 01:12:55.200
Okay?

1602
01:12:55.620 --> 01:12:57.040
Over Dwight's shoulder.

1603
01:12:58.000 --> 01:12:59.080
That's all I'm going to say.

1604
01:12:59.200 --> 01:13:02.220
Just enjoy that performance the next time you watch this scene.

1605
01:13:02.840 --> 01:13:03.860
It's wonderful.

1606
01:13:04.200 --> 01:13:05.320
Oh, my God, Jenna.

1607
01:13:05.320 --> 01:13:09.020
When we were all crammed around Kate's bed, that woman was there.

1608
01:13:10.280 --> 01:13:15.460
I swear, that woman, it was like she was a real patient.

1609
01:13:16.400 --> 01:13:21.320
She let out some kind of noise, and I thought we were all going to shit our pants.

1610
01:13:22.260 --> 01:13:27.760
She was a background actor, but she was so real.

1611
01:13:27.760 --> 01:13:36.280
Well, she literally, while we were standing there one time, went, like, I think they told her to maybe make a moaning sound.

1612
01:13:36.460 --> 01:13:36.820
Yeah.

1613
01:13:36.940 --> 01:13:40.140
And her interpretation of that, we went loopy.

1614
01:13:40.600 --> 01:13:43.780
Well, watch her in the background of the scene because she's excellent.

1615
01:13:44.060 --> 01:13:47.460
So now the doctor comes in, and Dwight has some questions for him.

1616
01:13:47.460 --> 01:13:51.800
And you and I both know that this is our writer, Justin Spitzer.

1617
01:13:52.960 --> 01:13:57.840
Yes, creator of some of your favorite Dwightisms, Justin Spitzer.

1618
01:13:58.000 --> 01:14:00.180
And the creator of the show, Superstore.

1619
01:14:00.520 --> 01:14:05.780
Well, I reached out to Justin, and he told me that he got this role after reading the part in the table read.

1620
01:14:06.680 --> 01:14:08.320
That he made Greg laugh.

1621
01:14:08.320 --> 01:14:10.660
Which Paul Lieberstein has shared that this would happen.

1622
01:14:10.660 --> 01:14:14.540
They wouldn't have some of the roles cast, and they would have writers read them.

1623
01:14:14.700 --> 01:14:20.400
And if a writer read a part, get ready, because Greg, there was a good chance Greg was going to put you in the show.

1624
01:14:20.580 --> 01:14:29.800
Well, he also told me that the look he gives to camera was actually him misunderstanding a piece of direction from Greg.

1625
01:14:29.980 --> 01:14:35.640
That Greg did not intend him to, like, perform that line to the camera as, like, a little joke.

1626
01:14:35.800 --> 01:14:37.300
Like, oh, so that's where it went.

1627
01:14:37.300 --> 01:14:39.020
He's talking about Meredith's uterus.

1628
01:14:39.180 --> 01:14:39.280
Yeah.

1629
01:14:40.860 --> 01:14:42.700
But Greg left it in.

1630
01:14:42.820 --> 01:14:43.720
I liked it.

1631
01:14:43.940 --> 01:14:45.060
I liked it, too.

1632
01:14:45.120 --> 01:14:46.620
But he said that was not the intention.

1633
01:14:46.620 --> 01:14:47.620
That was a mistake.

1634
01:14:47.960 --> 01:14:54.560
Well, we learn in this scene that Meredith has been bitten by a bat, which we knew.

1635
01:14:54.700 --> 01:15:00.560
But not only by a bat, but recently by a raccoon and a rat.

1636
01:15:00.740 --> 01:15:02.220
What the hell, Meredith?

1637
01:15:02.820 --> 01:15:04.220
What is she doing?

1638
01:15:04.220 --> 01:15:07.520
Honestly, a few of those animals could just live in her van.

1639
01:15:08.180 --> 01:15:08.920
Meredith's van.

1640
01:15:09.100 --> 01:15:09.400
Mm-hmm.

1641
01:15:09.900 --> 01:15:15.440
Well, when Dwight comes back from the hospital, he fills Michael in on all of this.

1642
01:15:15.720 --> 01:15:21.060
He says, you know, it turns out Meredith had been exposed to rabies.

1643
01:15:21.260 --> 01:15:22.660
Michael's like, ding, ding, ding, ding, ding.

1644
01:15:23.360 --> 01:15:29.180
And that going to the hospital might have saved her life because she got a rabies vaccine.

1645
01:15:29.340 --> 01:15:31.500
That is all Michael needed to hear.

1646
01:15:32.420 --> 01:15:36.780
He hit her with a car and saved her life.

1647
01:15:37.240 --> 01:15:37.920
Yes.

1648
01:15:38.160 --> 01:15:41.040
Now, he also says in this scene, Dwight says,

1649
01:15:41.040 --> 01:15:46.220
the only way to treat rabies is to start treatment before the symptoms start.

1650
01:15:47.120 --> 01:15:48.540
Well, I looked it up.

1651
01:15:48.740 --> 01:15:49.080
Mm-hmm.

1652
01:15:49.680 --> 01:15:50.760
This is true.

1653
01:15:51.880 --> 01:15:58.640
Did you know, Angela, that nearly 100% of people who develop symptoms die from rabies?

1654
01:15:59.300 --> 01:15:59.940
Die.

1655
01:16:00.420 --> 01:16:03.140
It cannot be cured once you get it.

1656
01:16:03.280 --> 01:16:04.320
I did not know that.

1657
01:16:04.880 --> 01:16:05.320
Yes.

1658
01:16:05.520 --> 01:16:10.600
So this is why you have to seek treatment immediately if you are ever bitten by an animal.

1659
01:16:10.740 --> 01:16:12.700
And a lot of animals can carry rabies.

1660
01:16:12.860 --> 01:16:16.020
But since I looked it up, I'll let you know that in the United States,

1661
01:16:16.020 --> 01:16:22.900
the most likely way to transmit rabies is through bats, coyotes, foxes, raccoons, and skunks.

1662
01:16:23.900 --> 01:16:27.500
In Africa and Southeast Asia, it is stray dogs.

1663
01:16:27.720 --> 01:16:28.700
I mean, what about monkeys?

1664
01:16:28.920 --> 01:16:32.800
There's parts of, like, Indonesia, like if you go up to Ubud, like, there's monkeys.

1665
01:16:32.800 --> 01:16:34.520
Like, all over the place.

1666
01:16:34.600 --> 01:16:34.880
Any animal bite.

1667
01:16:35.040 --> 01:16:37.860
If you get bitten by any animal, just go.

1668
01:16:38.160 --> 01:16:40.020
Go get a rabies vaccine.

1669
01:16:40.420 --> 01:16:41.700
It also said...

1670
01:16:41.700 --> 01:16:42.720
What about squirrels?

1671
01:16:43.780 --> 01:16:44.340
Yes!

1672
01:16:44.600 --> 01:16:45.540
Any animal.

1673
01:16:45.820 --> 01:16:47.540
If any animal bites you.

1674
01:16:47.680 --> 01:16:52.620
I'm just telling you the animals that are most likely to carry rabies in these locations.

1675
01:16:52.620 --> 01:16:55.440
But any animal can give it to you.

1676
01:16:55.540 --> 01:16:56.720
Is a mongoose on the list?

1677
01:16:58.420 --> 01:17:00.700
Is a mongoose any animal?

1678
01:17:02.560 --> 01:17:05.320
I'm just messing with you, but it's been really fun.

1679
01:17:07.960 --> 01:17:08.840
Well, listen.

1680
01:17:09.380 --> 01:17:11.760
Here is the thing that I found most interesting.

1681
01:17:11.760 --> 01:17:13.800
This is from the Mayo Clinic website.

1682
01:17:14.080 --> 01:17:15.180
Here's what it says.

1683
01:17:15.340 --> 01:17:15.720
Okay.

1684
01:17:16.340 --> 01:17:19.000
If you wake up in the morning...

1685
01:17:19.000 --> 01:17:19.200
Okay.

1686
01:17:19.660 --> 01:17:21.560
...and there's a bat in your room...

1687
01:17:21.560 --> 01:17:21.860
Okay.

1688
01:17:22.540 --> 01:17:24.380
...you should assume you've been bitten.

1689
01:17:25.280 --> 01:17:28.260
Because a bat can bite you without waking you up.

1690
01:17:29.160 --> 01:17:39.720
It also said, if you find a bat by a person who can't tell you that they've been bitten like a child or an impaired adult, assume they have also been bitten.

1691
01:17:40.460 --> 01:17:42.300
And go get a rabies vaccine.

1692
01:17:42.880 --> 01:17:45.760
Because once you show symptoms, there is no cure.

1693
01:17:46.500 --> 01:17:52.820
Well, I was watching an episode of Our Planet, and they were talking about these baby seals.

1694
01:17:53.380 --> 01:17:57.060
And there are vampire bats that go and try to just suck their blood.

1695
01:17:57.200 --> 01:17:58.380
And they can hop.

1696
01:17:59.760 --> 01:18:00.740
They hop around.

1697
01:18:00.760 --> 01:18:01.780
The seals or the bats?

1698
01:18:01.840 --> 01:18:02.800
The bats!

1699
01:18:04.000 --> 01:18:04.960
They jump.

1700
01:18:04.960 --> 01:18:06.320
I'm going to send you a video.

1701
01:18:06.320 --> 01:18:07.100
They hop.

1702
01:18:07.320 --> 01:18:09.960
And they are bloodsuckers.

1703
01:18:10.300 --> 01:18:11.640
They hop and bite.

1704
01:18:11.760 --> 01:18:12.500
They hop and bite.

1705
01:18:15.640 --> 01:18:16.120
Yeah.

1706
01:18:16.420 --> 01:18:18.780
Well, there you go, guys.

1707
01:18:18.860 --> 01:18:19.420
There you go.

1708
01:18:19.440 --> 01:18:22.800
That's your rabies cheat sheet.

1709
01:18:22.940 --> 01:18:25.180
That's everything you ever wanted to know about rabies.

1710
01:18:25.200 --> 01:18:27.900
Basically, if you get bit by an animal, that's what I learned.

1711
01:18:27.960 --> 01:18:29.320
Get that rabies shot.

1712
01:18:30.040 --> 01:18:30.520
Good!

1713
01:18:30.720 --> 01:18:31.480
Oh, yes!

1714
01:18:31.480 --> 01:18:33.340
That was the takeaway I was hoping for.

1715
01:18:33.340 --> 01:18:34.040
Well, there you go.

1716
01:18:34.400 --> 01:18:35.900
Well, Michael is thrilled.

1717
01:18:36.320 --> 01:18:38.480
To find out that he has saved Meredith's life.

1718
01:18:38.600 --> 01:18:38.920
Oh, yeah.

1719
01:18:39.120 --> 01:18:40.200
He walks into the bullpen.

1720
01:18:40.340 --> 01:18:43.520
He declares that the curse has been broken.

1721
01:18:43.880 --> 01:18:45.520
Turns out there is a God.

1722
01:18:47.080 --> 01:18:48.340
Everything is great.

1723
01:18:48.660 --> 01:18:50.060
But who is Jesus' dad?

1724
01:18:52.080 --> 01:18:53.840
Yeah, he's not sure, I guess.

1725
01:18:54.240 --> 01:19:02.080
And meanwhile, Kevin, you know, has been on the case this whole episode trying to figure out if Jim and Pam are dating.

1726
01:19:02.080 --> 01:19:05.360
He's positive that they are, but it's the end of the day.

1727
01:19:05.380 --> 01:19:06.260
And he's like, you know what?

1728
01:19:06.440 --> 01:19:07.660
I guess they're not together.

1729
01:19:07.700 --> 01:19:09.380
And now they probably never will be.

1730
01:19:09.500 --> 01:19:13.100
And it's too bad because they're like PB and J.

1731
01:19:13.100 --> 01:19:15.380
Hey, Pam Beasley and Jim.

1732
01:19:16.460 --> 01:19:17.020
Yeah.

1733
01:19:17.300 --> 01:19:24.480
And that was an inside joke because at this point, fans of the show had started calling Jim and Pam Jam.

1734
01:19:24.920 --> 01:19:25.460
Yes.

1735
01:19:25.740 --> 01:19:27.800
They had mashed our names as Jam.

1736
01:19:27.800 --> 01:19:33.980
And so it was this funny thing that Kevin would call us PB and J and not Jam.

1737
01:19:34.040 --> 01:19:35.200
A little nod to the fans.

1738
01:19:35.620 --> 01:19:36.480
A little nod.

1739
01:19:37.100 --> 01:19:38.380
Well, you know what?

1740
01:19:38.380 --> 01:19:40.020
We see Pam leave for the day.

1741
01:19:40.320 --> 01:19:41.120
She gets in her car.

1742
01:19:41.280 --> 01:19:41.980
She drives away.

1743
01:19:42.140 --> 01:19:43.100
She's by herself.

1744
01:19:44.600 --> 01:19:52.080
Clearly, the documentary crew is as suspicious as Kevin because they follow her as she drives off.

1745
01:19:52.260 --> 01:19:56.140
It made me wonder, my gosh, how long do they follow us after we leave work?

1746
01:19:56.220 --> 01:19:59.840
Well, I don't think you should be that worried because Pam doesn't drive very far.

1747
01:20:00.780 --> 01:20:02.980
I was like, Pam, do better.

1748
01:20:02.980 --> 01:20:06.540
You drove like four car lengths and then you pulled over.

1749
01:20:06.800 --> 01:20:07.660
And then what?

1750
01:20:07.820 --> 01:20:09.460
